      "caveats": "The abstract provides a high-level historical and cultural overview rather than empirical, quantitative measurements of specific mitigation outcomes.",
      "what": "This paper analyzes Japan's historical and contemporary culture of disaster preparedness, focusing on how design, architecture, and urban planning are integrated to mitigate risks from earthquakes, typhoons, and flooding.",
      "why": "It documents a comprehensive national model where disaster resilience is embedded directly into daily spatial design and cultural practices, rather than treated solely as an emergency response measure."
